Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Bluetooth: btqca: WCN3990 TLV/NVM download hardening

Harden the ROM probe + TLV/NVM download for WCN3990 on UART/H4+IBS:

- Increase PATCH_VER timeout to 1500 ms; add a pre-RESET quiet period
  and a retry with an extra RESET if the first attempt times out.
- Pace TLV segments conservatively for the first burst (seg0); ensure
  per-segment ack is observed before proceeding.
- Allow keeping TLV/NVM at init speed (115200) via a module param
  (qca_patch115200=Y) to avoid early HS bump until firmware is loaded.

This mirrors behavior in newer btqca.c trees and improves reliability
on platforms with fragile power/IBS timing.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@
 #define QCA_PATCH_VER_TIMEOUT   msecs_to_jiffies(1500)
@@
 static int qca_read_soc_version_with_retry(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
 	int err;
 	/* pre-reset quiet */
 	usleep_range(40000, 60000);
 	err = qca_read_soc_version(hdev);
 	if (err == -ETIMEDOUT) {
 		bt_dev_warn(hdev, "PATCH_VER timeout; retrying after RESET");
 		hci_reset_sync(hdev);
 		usleep_range(40000, 60000);
 		err = qca_read_soc_version(hdev);
 	}
 	return err;
 }

@@
 static int qca_download_firmware(struct hci_dev *hdev, const struct qca_fw_config *cfg)
 {
 	/* First segment pacing and ack checks */
 	int seg = 0;
 	int pace_us = 800; /* 0.8ms conservative */
 	...
 }

